So to catch {f:her|his} interest, you'll sometimes need to play it cold.
{f:Apparently your sweetheart|All right,} {f:goes for the cool type of guy|give it a try right away}.
{f:Love is all strategy,|And if it doesn't work out,} {f:hyahyahyahyahya|you can just throw yourself into my arms}.{p}

{f:Hmm|Huh}, {f:you poor thing...|that's odd.}
{f:Guess you're just not popular|I'm sure that can't be right}.
{f:But it can't be helped, so|At least I, for one,} {f:let's try divining something else|am head over heels for you}.
{f:Come on|Well then}, {f:which one will it be|shall we move on}?{p}

Did you have a fight with {f:her|him} recently or something?
{f:It seems you're|This is fate too,} {f:destined to be dumped|but don't let it get you down}.
{f:It's sad, but that's how it goes.|You've still got me, haven't you?}
...I know, try divining something else.
Come on, which one will it be?{p}

{f:But you|See,} {f:can't break up with her, can you|it all adds up, doesn't it}?
{f:After all,|Oh man,} {f:you said you liked her|this is great}.
{f:...Couples like this|I bet we'll} {f:sure are common these days|make the best couple ever}.
{f:Hey,|My} {f:don't be so down.|honey...}
I know, why don't you try divining something else?
Come on, which one will it be?{p}

Ah, it came out well.
Good, good.
From today on, spend your money with a proper plan{f:, okay|, you hear}?{p}

All right then, let me see whether you'll become rich.
Kokkuri-san, Kokkuri-san, please answer us.
Will {c}{f:|} become rich in the future?{p}

See, just as I thought, it looks like you have enemies.
While we're at it, I'll divine what kind of person it is, too.
Kokkuri-san, Kokkuri-san, what kind of person will be {c}{f:|}'s enemy?{p}

Broke, huh...
How awful.
Well, even if you're broke now, you might make it big someday, so let's divine that.{p}

Kokkuri-san, Kokkuri-san, please answer us.
If {c}{f:|} gets that job, will it be a success?
Please tell us how it will turn out.{p}

{f:Hurry up and study, then|You'd better hurry up and study}.
{f:A guy who slacks off|If you'll have me,} {f:won't be popular with girls|I'll teach you anything you like}.
{f:Well, I'll check anyway|Oh, I know,} {f:whether you'll get that job someday, but...|why don't I become your private tutor from now on?}
{f:With an attitude like that,|Heh heh heh,} {f:you may not get a good result|this is going to be fun}.{p}

Next... let's see, let's read about the walls you'll have to get over to make your dream come true.
Kokkuri-san, Kokkuri-san, please answer.
Would you tell us what will hold {c}{f:|} back from making that dream real?{p}

Ah, it says you'll be torn between love and your dream.
Do you put your lover first, or your dream...?
That's a tough one.
But it says you'll make your dream come true, so what becomes of your lover then...
{f:Well, I hope you can have it all|If I were the one, though, you'd have it all}: your dream and your love{f:, both of them.|. I'd never make you give up either.}
Now, what shall we read next?{p}

Hmm, looks like the walls the world puts up are thick.
No matter what people say to you, keep at it.
So, what shall we read next?{p}

Life is full of all sorts of mountains and valleys and rivers and forests and woods and birds and flowers and butterflies.
...You don't get what I'm saying?
Oh well. So, what shall we read next?{p}

Next... let's see, let's read about the people who'll help you make that dream real.
Kokkuri-san, Kokkuri-san, please answer.
Who on earth will help {c}{f:|} with that dream?{p}

It says your lover will be a big support to you.
I wonder what they're like.
Is there anyone you'd think of that way right now?
If not, I guess they'll show up later on.
{f:Honestly|Or wait}, {f:you're one|maybe it's the one right in front of you}{f: lucky devil.|: me.}
So, what shall we read next?{p}

Very well, then I shall divine it for you.
Kokkuri-san, Kokkuri-san, please answer.
Will {c}{f:|} live a fun, carefree life in the future?{p}

Mm, very well, I shall divine it for you.
Kokkuri-san, Kokkuri-san, please answer.
Will {c}{f:|} get to lead a turbulent life in the future?{p}

I see. Then I shall divine it for you.
Kokkuri-san, Kokkuri-san, please answer.
Will {c}{f:|} be able to live a stable, steady life in the future?{p}

...Don't give me such a scary look.
{f:I'm kidding|You're hurting my feelings}.
{f:Like I'd ever lend|And here I was, all set} {f:my chest to a guy.|to hold you tight.}{p}

Leave me alone.
Never mind about me.
If you've got nothing else you want to ask, I'm going to ask Kokkuri-san to leave.{p}
